assets.notes:
Fix round: the leather box3 now covers only the sprung saddle and the last 0.08 m of each grip (x -0.168 to -0.06, from tools/geo.py). The handlebar and stem are steel, so the chrome bars read grey with a lit top. The 12x9 steel block at the bottom bracket is erased. In its place, drawn after the outline as props.js bicycle() does, are:
- a chainring r 5.5: steel[5] rim lit at the upper left, steel[2] lower right, a steel[3] band, steel[1] middle and a steel[4] crank boss;
- two chain runs to the rear hub, with links alternating steel[2] / steel[4];
- a 2 px crank and an 8x2 pedal.
The chain, crank and pedal have no outline, like the spokes. 94x65 px. The Unreal model is good.

judge.notes:
No credits; T3D failed twice, so no more Meshy spend.
(1) Hinge collar (sprite x 174-200, y 4-22): an unlit near-black coal mass with a knobby outline. Replace it with a drawn hub:
- a clean 10x10 px cylinder in coal[3], with a coal[5] top row and left column and coal[1] on the bottom and right;
- a 3x3 steel[5] axle cap with a steel[2] shadow pixel;
- a 1 px coal[1] shadow onto the pole;
- a straight silhouette, no knobs.
(2) Counterweight (x 214-233, y 5-26): the two bolt heads side by side read as eyes. Use one centred bolt, or bolts at the lower corners, each a coal[5] / coal[1] pair.
(3) Pivot post (x 198-210, y 20-62): give it a continuous steel[5] lit left column from top to bottom instead of the single glint. Do the same on the rest post, whose lit edge is broken into dashes.
(4) Record in the kit notes that boom_arm.glb is procedural: the Meshy refine contributed only the posts.
Kit: ok (origin at the axle; bands 0.4 m from the tip).
